# VoiceVision Backends - Overview
# Source: src/voicevision/backends/

## MoondreamBackend (vision.py)
- GGUF via llama.cpp (ADR-001, ADR-002)
- Stateless, no close()
- Uses supervised llama-server on port 8081
- Models: moondream2-text-model-f16.gguf + mmproj

## WhisperCppBackend (whisper_cpp.py)
- whisper.cpp CLI one-shot subprocess
- Reads WAV from stdin, writes transcript to stdout
- Supports --detect-language for auto language detection
- Model path required via VOICEVISION_STT_MODEL
- Validation: 16kHz mono PCM16 WAV only

## LlamaCppBackend (llama_cpp.py)
- Supervised llama-server daemon (persistent)
- Model loaded once, reused across calls
- Streaming via complete_stream() yields tokens
- Port 8080 default
- Model path via VOICEVISION_LLM_MODEL

## PiperBackend (piper.py)
- Piper TTS CLI
- CURRENTLY BROKEN: voice.onnx.json is empty/corrupt
- PiperVoice.load() fails
- Needs valid piper voice model + JSON config
- Model path via VOICEVISION_TTS_MODEL, voice via VOICEVISION_TTS_VOICE

## WebrtcVadBackend (vad.py)
- WebRTC VAD via webrtcvad-wheels
- 16kHz mono, 30ms frames
- Aggressiveness 0-3 (default 2)
- Returns utterance (start, end) byte offsets